/* data/learn-c/cs-12-04.js - GENERATED by tools/build_learn.py from data/learn/summaries/cs-12-04.json (our own words;
 * the notes of one chapter, loaded when the chapter is opened). Do not edit by hand. */
(window.LEARN_C = window.LEARN_C || {})["cs-12-04"] = {"1":{"s":"HTML (Hyper Text Markup Language) is the language used to make web pages. A page is written with tags that tell the browser how to show text, pictures, links and tables. The Internet is a worldwide network of networks; the www is the collection of web pages on it, joined by links, and a web browser fetches and shows them. A page has the html tag, a head part with a title, and a body part.","w":["HTML is a markup language: it describes how the page looks; it is not a programming language.","The title in the head part shows in the title bar of the browser, not in the page area."],"x":["HTML is the language for web pages. It uses tags, which are words in angle brackets, to tell the browser how to show the content. Most tags come in pairs, a start tag and an end tag; a few, like the line break and the horizontal rule, have no end tag. Tag names are not case sensitive.","The Internet is a worldwide network that joins many networks. The www (World Wide Web) is a service on it: a huge set of web pages, joined by hyperlinks, kept on web servers. A web browser, like Chrome or Firefox, finds a page by its address (URL), reads its HTML and shows it.","The structure of a page: the html tag holds everything; the head part comes first and holds the title; the body part holds all that is shown in the window. A page is written in a plain text editor and saved with the extension html or htm."],"e":"A smallest page: the html tag, a head with the title My page, and a body that says Hello. Saved as hello.html and opened in a browser, it shows Hello and the title in the title bar."},"2":{"s":"HTML is used because it is simple, free, platform independent and supported by every browser; pages are small and load fast, and links join pages. It can show text, pictures, tables, sound and video. Its limitations are that pages are static, it cannot calculate or take decisions by itself, it gives no real security, and different browsers may show a page a little differently.","w":["Static means the page does not change by itself; scripts (such as VB script) are added to make it dynamic.","HTML alone cannot do calculations."],"x":["Advantages: HTML is easy to learn and a page can be written in any text editor. It is free and works on all computers and browsers (platform independent). Pages are light and load quickly. Hyperlinks join pages and sites. It can show text, pictures, tables, sound and video.","Limitations: HTML makes static pages; it cannot do calculations or take decisions. It has no real security for the data of a page. A big site needs a lot of repeated code, and it is hard to keep the same style on many pages. Browsers may show the same page a little differently.","To remove the main limitation, HTML pages are combined with scripts, which are small programs that run in the browser."],"e":"An online result page written only in HTML can show the marks, but it cannot work out the percentage when the user enters the marks. A script is needed for that."},"3":{"s":"Important tags: html, head, title, body; p (paragraph, with align), br (line break), hr (horizontal line), h1 to h6 (headings), b, i and u (bold, italic, underline), em (emphasis), li inside ul or ol (lists), a with href (link), sup and sub, pre (keeps spaces) and marquee (scrolling text). The ul tag gives bullets and the ol tag gives numbers, and their type attribute changes the style.","w":["The br and hr tags are empty tags; they need no end tag.","Use the ul tag for bullets and the ol tag for numbers. The li tag is for each item in both."],"x":["The head part has the title tag. In the body, the p tag starts a paragraph (with a blank line before it) and its align attribute can be left, center or right. The br tag breaks the line without a blank line. The hr tag draws a horizontal line (attributes: width, size, align, noshade). The headings h1 to h6 go from the biggest to the smallest.","Formatting tags: b makes text bold, i italic and u underlined; em marks emphasis (a logical tag), while b only changes the look (a physical tag). The sup tag raises text and the sub tag lowers it, as in x squared and H2O. The pre tag shows text exactly as typed, with its spaces and lines. The marquee tag makes text scroll.","Lists: the ul tag makes an unordered (bulleted) list with the type disc, circle or square; the ol tag makes an ordered (numbered) list with type 1, A, a, I or i and the start attribute. Each item is written with the li tag (its value attribute sets a number). A link is made with the a tag and its href attribute, which gives the address; for e-mail the href begins with mailto."],"e":"A shopping list: an ol tag with type A, and three li items: Rice, Milk, Fruit. The browser shows A. Rice, B. Milk, C. Fruit."},"4":{"s":"The font tag changes the look of text with the attributes size (1 to 7), color (a name or an RGB code) and face (the name of the font). The big and small tags make text larger or smaller than the text around it. The b, i and u tags make text bold, italic and underlined; sub and sup lower and raise text. An RGB code is a hash with six hexadecimal digits, two each for red, green and blue.","w":["Yellow is the RGB code FFFF00: red and green full, no blue.","The font size attribute goes from 1 (smallest) to 7 (biggest)."],"x":["The font tag changes the way text is shown. Its size attribute takes a value from 1 to 7 (3 is the normal size); the color attribute takes a colour name or an RGB code; the face attribute names the typeface. The big and small tags make the text a step bigger or smaller.","Colours on a screen are mixed from red, green and blue light. An RGB code is written as a hash and six hexadecimal digits: two for red, two for green and two for blue, each from 00 to FF. So FF0000 is red, 00FF00 is green, 0000FF is blue, FFFF00 is yellow (red and green), FFFFFF is white and 000000 is black.","These tags can be combined, but they must be closed in the reverse order of opening: bold and italic together are written b, i, text, end i, end b."],"e":"To show the word Warning in red, bigger text: use the font tag with color equal to the code FF0000 and size 5 around the word."},"5":{"s":"The img tag puts a picture in a page. It is an empty tag. Its src attribute gives the picture file; alt gives text shown if the picture cannot load (and read by screen readers); height and width set the size; border sets a frame; align places the picture (top, middle, bottom, left or right). An inline image sits in the line of text; a floating image goes to the left or right and the text flows around it.","w":["The alt attribute is for when the picture does not load, and for blind users.","An inline image uses no align; a floating image uses align left or right."],"x":["The img tag shows a picture. It has no end tag. The src attribute gives the name or address of the picture file. The alt attribute gives alternate text: it is shown if the picture cannot be loaded or the browser does not show pictures, it is read by screen readers for blind users, and it appears as a tip on the picture. Height and width set the size in pixels, and border sets a frame around it.","The align attribute decides where the picture is in relation to the text: top, middle and bottom put the text along the picture at that position; left and right move the picture to that margin and let the text flow around it (a floating image).","An inline image is placed inside the line of text like a big letter. A floating image is moved to a margin with align left or right, and the text wraps around it."],"e":"An img tag with src equal to logo.jpg, alt equal to College logo, and align equal to left puts the logo at the left margin with the text flowing on its right."},"6":{"s":"A table is made with the table tag. Each row is a tr tag; inside a row, th makes a bold centred heading cell and td makes a data cell. The caption tag gives the table a title. The table attributes include border, cellpadding (space inside a cell), cellspacing (space between cells), width, height, align and bgcolor. The colspan attribute makes a cell go across columns and rowspan makes it go down across rows.","w":["Without the border attribute the table has no lines.","Colspan joins columns and rowspan joins rows; the covered cells are left out of the code."],"x":["The table tag holds the whole table. A row is written with the tr tag. Inside a row a heading cell is made with th (bold and centred by default) and a data cell with td. The caption tag, written just after the table tag, gives a title. The border attribute draws lines (without it there are none), cellpadding sets the space between the text and the cell border, and cellspacing sets the space between cells; width, height, align and bgcolor set size, place and background colour.","Colspan makes one cell go across several columns, for example a heading Year over three columns. Rowspan makes one cell go down across several rows, for example the word Sale beside two rows. When a cell spans, the cells it covers are left out in the other rows or columns, so the number of cells in each row must still add up.","To write a table: plan the rows and columns on paper, write one tr for each row, put th or td for each cell, and add colspan and rowspan where cells join."],"e":"A 2 by 2 table of marks: a table tag with border 1, a first tr with two th cells (Subject, Marks) and a second tr with two td cells (Maths, 90)."},"7":{"s":"A script is a small program written inside a web page that the browser runs. It makes the page dynamic: it can calculate, take decisions, check forms and show messages. It is written between the script tags with the language set to VBScript. The syllabus covers For next, If then else, message boxes (MsgBox), input boxes (InputBox), and the Dim and Set statements.","w":["HTML cannot calculate; a script is added for that.","A variable in VBScript is declared with Dim."],"x":["A script is a program inside a web page. The browser runs it, so the page can respond: it can do calculations, take decisions, check what the user typed and show messages. This makes the page dynamic. VBScript is a scripting language like Visual Basic.","A script is written between the script start and end tags, with the language attribute giving VBScript. A variable is declared with Dim. The If then else statement takes decisions, the For next statement repeats a block, MsgBox shows a message box, InputBox asks the user to type a value, and Set gives a value to an object variable. document.write puts text in the page.","Advantages: it makes pages interactive, it can check a form on the user computer so the server is not troubled, and it is easy to learn."],"e":"A script that makes a random digit for each visit uses Randomize, then n = Int(Rnd times 10), and document.write(n) shows a digit from 0 to 9."}};
